 "preamble": "Solutions to eight of the across clues must have two adjacent letters replaced before entry in the grid. The wordplay of their clues leads to the altered version to be entered. The misprints involved are from a set of eight displaced from the usual positions. Wordplay in the other eight across clues contains a superfluous letter that should be ignored. These eight letters in order, with the inclusion of a ninth letter to be deduced and entered in the centre of the grid, spell out the name of a person who admitted to perhaps having the set of eight in the wrong order. All down clues and solutions are normal.",
